claim.claim-text:
receiving, from a base station, configuration information including information on resource allocation for physical uplink shared channel, PUSCH, transmission in a time domain, and information indicating a PUSCH repetition;
identifying, based on the configuration information, whether the UE is configured with the PUSCH repetition across slot boundary in consecutive slots;
identifying whether a symbol to be dropped for the PUSCH repetition exists among symbols in a slot; and
in case that the UE is configured with the PUSCH repetition across the slot boundary in the consecutive slots, transmitting a repetition of the PUSCH transmission comprising a first part and a second part, wherein the first part of the repetition is allocated in a slot n and the second part of the repetition is allocated in slot n+1,
wherein the repetition of the PUSCH transmission is performed in a unit of a number of symbols less than or equal to a number of symbols constituting one slot, and
wherein the symbol to be dropped includes a downlink symbol for downlink transmission.

transmitting, to a user equipment, UE, configuration information including information on resource allocation for physical uplink shared channel, PUSCH, transmission in a time domain, and information indicating a PUSCH repetition;
identifying, based on the configuration information, whether the UE is configured with the PUSCH repetition across slot boundary in consecutive slots;
identifying whether a symbol to be dropped for the PUSCH repetition exists among symbols in a slot; and
in case that the UE is configured with the PUSCH repetition across the slot boundary in the consecutive slots, receiving a repetition of the PUSCH transmission comprising a first part and a second part, wherein the first part of the repetition is allocated in a slot n and the second part of the repetition is allocated in slot n+1,
wherein the repetition of the PUSCH transmission is configured in a unit of a number of symbols less than or equal to a number of symbols constituting one slot, and
wherein the symbol to be dropped includes a downlink symbol for downlink transmission.
